  "answer": "Fixed `normalizeText` in `normalize.mjs`.\n\n**Change made:** Added `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` between `.trim()` and `.toLowerCase()`.\n\n**Why it satisfies the spec:**\n- **Non-string input** → still throws `TypeError` (unchanged guard).\n- **Leading/trailing whitespace** → removed by `.trim()` (handles spaces, tabs, line breaks, and all JS whitespace).\n- **Internal whitespace runs** → `/\\s+/g` matches each nonempty run of JS whitespace and replaces it with a single ASCII space. Since trimming happens first, no leading/trailing space is introduced.\n- **Lowercasing** → `.toLowerCase()` via `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`.\n- **Empty/whitespace-only input** → `.trim()` yields `''`, the regex finds no matches, and the result is `''`.\n\nThe named export `normalizeText` and the public tests are untouched.",
